(*=============================================================================
  BrighterScript Grammar (EBNF)  --  the `.bs` superset layered on BrightScript
=============================================================================

  WHAT THIS IS
  ------------
  A grammar for BrighterScript (`.bs`), the RokuCommunity language superset that
  transpiles to plain BrightScript (`.brs`). It is authored as a thin DELTA on
  top of the sibling spec `brightscript.ebnf`: it IMPORTS that grammar and
  REDEFINES only the handful of "seam" productions that BrighterScript extends
  (the expression cascade entry, the type grammar, Primary, the postfix-suffix
  set, associative-array entries, assignment, for-each), then adds the brand-new
  declaration/expression/type productions on top. Everything BrighterScript
  shares with BrightScript (statements, the operator-precedence cascade, literals,
  comments, conditional compilation, blocks, parameters) is referenced by name and
  inherited unchanged. A locally redefined rule SHADOWS the imported one -- this
  is true grammar override, so e.g. an inherited `if` condition automatically
  admits a BrighterScript ternary because `Expression` is overridden here.

  This mirrors the relationship in the project:
      brightscript.ebnf  --(imported, pristine)-->  brighterscript.ebnf
  exactly as scenegraph.ebnf embeds brightscript.ebnf -- except SceneGraph embeds
  BrightScript as an opaque text region (language injection), whereas
  BrighterScript is a genuine SUPERSET that weaves new alternatives into the base
  grammar (so it OVERRIDES seam rules rather than treating them as a black box).

  SCOPE  (per the 05 initiative: "spec exhaustive, validation grows")
  -----
  This file models the FULL BrighterScript language surface that the compiler
  accepts -- every BrighterScript-only statement, expression, type form, literal,
  and annotation -- not just the angel-roku-evidenced subset. The harness corpus
  and on-device validation start at the real-world subset (namespace / class /
  annotations / dotted names, which angel-roku uses pervasively) and grow from
  there; the grammar itself is complete.

  SOURCE / AUTHORITY
  ------------------
  The canonical authority for the language is the BrighterScript compiler source
  (rokucommunity/brighterscript). PINNED VERSION: 0.72.2 -- this is both the
  installed `bsc` (the syntax ground-truth, `npm run check`) AND the `master`
  HEAD at authoring time, so the modeled surface is exactly what this `bsc`
  accepts. Each construct below cites the parser/lexer symbol it was mined from:
    - Tokens / keyword sets ........ src/lexer/TokenKind.ts
                                     (Keywords, AllowedProperties,
                                      AllowedLocalIdentifiers, DeclarableTypes,
                                      BrighterScriptSourceLiterals, the
                                      `brighterscript keywords` block)
    - Lexing (templates, regex, @) . src/lexer/Lexer.ts
    - Accepted syntax .............. src/parser/Parser.ts (method names cited)
    - AST node set ................. src/parser/Statement.ts, Expression.ts,
                                     src/astUtils/reflection.ts
    - Type spelling ................ src/parser/Parser.ts typeToken(),
                                     src/util.ts tokenToBscType, src/types/*
  Real-world usage corpus / regression target: ../angel-roku (52 authored `.bs`
  rooibos test modules). Constructs it exercises are called out with an
  "angel-roku:" note in their rule comments below.

  GROUND TRUTH = BOTH (the 05 model):
    - `bsc` 0.72.2 is the authority for whether `.bs` SYNTAX is accepted.
    - the Roku DEVICE (transpile `.bs` -> `.brs` -> sideload -> `##SPEC##`) is
      the authority for whether the lowered code RUNS. Where they disagree the
      device wins and the drift is logged in BSC_DRIFT.md / DEVICE_FACTS.md.

  Date: 2026-05-20

  EBNF NOTATION  (identical to brightscript.ebnf / scenegraph.ebnf)
  -------------
  Name ::= expr | A B alternation | ( ) group | A? opt | A* star | A+ plus
  'literal'/"literal" terminal (CASE-INSENSITIVE, like BrightScript) ·
  [a-z] char class · A - B exception · #x000A hex code · block comments use the
  same delimiter style as the sibling specs.
  UpperCamelCase = syntactic rule; UPPER_SNAKE = lexical token.

  IMPORTED NAMES  (defined in brightscript.ebnf, referenced but not redefined)
  --------------
  Lexical tokens:  Identifier StringLiteral Literal Char LINE_BREAK EOS
                   AT DOT LPAREN RPAREN LBRACKET RBRACKET LBRACE RBRACE
                   COMMA COLON ASSIGN QUESTION OP_OR
  Declarations:    FunctionDeclaration SubDeclaration LibraryStatement
                   ParameterList ReturnType Block
  Statements:      Statement Label Comment ConstDirective ConditionalCompilation
                   AssignTarget
  Expressions:     OrExpr  (entry into the inherited precedence cascade)
                   ParenExpr ArrayLiteral AssocArrayLiteral AnonymousFunction
                   CreateObjectCall BuiltinCall ArgumentList
                   CallSuffix IndexSuffix MemberSuffix AttributeSuffix
                   OptChainSuffix AAKey ElementSep
  The cascade OrExpr -> AndExpr -> ... -> PostfixExpr -> Primary is inherited;
  because Primary / PostfixSuffix / AAEntry are OVERRIDDEN below, the inherited
  cascade automatically reaches the BrighterScript primary/postfix forms.

  REDEFINED ("seam") PRODUCTIONS shadowing brightscript.ebnf:
    TopLevelItem · Expression · Type · Primary · PostfixSuffix · AAEntry ·
    AssignmentStatement · ForEachStatement
=============================================================================*)


(*===========================================================================*)
(*  PART 1 - PROGRAM STRUCTURE & TOP-LEVEL ITEMS                              *)
(*===========================================================================*)

(* A `.bs` source file. Same shape as brightscript SourceFile but the top-level
   item set is the BrighterScript-extended one (TopLevelItem, redefined below).
   src/parser/Parser.ts: parse() / body(). *)
BrighterScriptSourceFile ::= EOS? ( TopLevelItem ( EOS TopLevelItem )* )? EOS?

(* OVERRIDE of brightscript.ebnf TopLevelItem: adds the BrighterScript-only
   top-level declarations and annotation-prefixed declarations, then falls
   through to the inherited BrightScript top-level alternatives (referenced by
   their sub-production names so no `TopLevelItem` self-reference is needed).
   src/parser/Parser.ts: declaration(). *)
TopLevelItem    ::= AnnotatedItem
                  | NamespaceStatement
                  | ClassDeclaration
                  | InterfaceDeclaration
                  | EnumDeclaration
                  | ConstStatement
                  | ImportStatement
                  | TypecastStatement
                  | AliasStatement
                  | TypeAliasStatement
                  (* --- inherited BrightScript top-level alternatives --- *)
                  | FunctionDeclaration
                  | SubDeclaration
                  | LibraryStatement
                  | ConstDirective
                  | ConditionalCompilation
                  | Comment
                  | Label
                  | Statement

(*--- 1.1 Annotations ------------------------------------------------------*)

(* `@Name` or `@Name(args)` compile-time metadata attached to the FOLLOWING
   declaration; stripped on transpile. The arg list is a real call-argument list
   (any expressions, incl. AA literals). BrighterScript-only.
   src/parser/Parser.ts: annotationExpression(); src/parser/Expression.ts:
   AnnotationExpression. angel-roku: @it/@describe/@suite/@tags/@beforeeach.
   LEXER: the `@` here is the AT token at statement start; mid-expression `@.`
   is the callfunc operator and `@`/`?@` are XML-attribute access -- see note 2. *)
AnnotatedItem   ::= ( Annotation EOS )+ AnnotatableDeclaration
Annotation      ::= AT Identifier ( LPAREN ArgumentList? RPAREN )?
AnnotatableDeclaration ::= NamespaceStatement
                  | ClassDeclaration
                  | InterfaceDeclaration
                  | EnumDeclaration
                  | ConstStatement
                  | FunctionDeclaration
                  | SubDeclaration

(*--- 1.2 Qualified (dotted / namespaced) names ----------------------------*)

(* A dotted name reference: `a`, `a.b`, `pkg.sub.Thing`. Used for namespace
   names, `extends` parents, `new` targets, and custom type names. The runtime
   reference `a.b.c` itself is just an inherited DottedGet chain (MemberSuffix);
   this production is for the declaration/type positions that require a name.
   src/parser/Expression.ts: NamespacedVariableNameExpression. angel-roku:
   `extends rooibos.BaseTestSuite`, `tests.foo()`. *)
QualifiedName   ::= Identifier ( DOT Identifier )*


(*===========================================================================*)
(*  PART 2 - NAMESPACE / CLASS / INTERFACE / ENUM DECLARATIONS               *)
(*===========================================================================*)

(*--- 2.1 Namespace --------------------------------------------------------*)

(* `namespace A.B ... end namespace`. Members are namespaced declarations.
   BrighterScript-only. src/parser/Parser.ts: namespaceStatement().
   angel-roku: 52/52 authored .bs files open with a namespace. *)
NamespaceStatement ::= 'namespace' QualifiedName EOS
                          NamespaceBody?
                       ( ( 'end' 'namespace' ) | 'endnamespace' )
NamespaceBody   ::= ( NamespaceMember EOS )* NamespaceMember?
NamespaceMember ::= AnnotatedItem
                  | NamespaceStatement
                  | ClassDeclaration
                  | InterfaceDeclaration
                  | EnumDeclaration
                  | ConstStatement
                  | FunctionDeclaration
                  | SubDeclaration
                  | Comment
                  | ConditionalCompilation

(*--- 2.2 Class ------------------------------------------------------------*)

(* `class Name [extends Qualified] ... end class`. Members are fields and
   methods, each optionally annotated and access-modified. BrighterScript-only.
   src/parser/Parser.ts: classDeclaration(). angel-roku: 47 class decls,
   15 `super`, 23 `override`, 38 `private`, 25 `protected`. *)
ClassDeclaration ::= 'class' Identifier ( 'extends' QualifiedName )? EOS
                        ClassBody?
                     ( ( 'end' 'class' ) | 'endclass' )
ClassBody       ::= ( ClassMember EOS )* ClassMember?
ClassMember     ::= AnnotatedClassMember
                  | FieldDeclaration
                  | MethodDeclaration
                  | Comment
                  | ConditionalCompilation
AnnotatedClassMember ::= ( Annotation EOS )+ ( FieldDeclaration | MethodDeclaration )

(* Field: `[access] [optional] name [as Type] [= initializer]`.
   src/parser/Parser.ts: fieldDeclaration(); Statement.ts: FieldStatement. *)
FieldDeclaration ::= AccessModifier? 'optional'? Identifier
                        ( 'as' Type )? ( ASSIGN Expression )?

(* Method: `[access] [override] (function|sub) ...`. Reuses the inherited
   function/sub declaration (their bodies + params + return type are inherited;
   `as CustomType` becomes valid via the Type override). The constructor is a
   method named `new` (`override` is rejected on it -- a semantic, not a parse,
   rule). src/parser/Parser.ts: classDeclaration() method branch;
   Statement.ts: MethodStatement. *)
MethodDeclaration ::= AccessModifier? 'override'? ( FunctionDeclaration | SubDeclaration )

AccessModifier  ::= 'public' | 'protected' | 'private'

(*--- 2.3 Interface --------------------------------------------------------*)

(* `interface Name [extends Qualified] ... end interface`. Members are typed
   field and method SIGNATURES (no bodies). BrighterScript-only.
   src/parser/Parser.ts: interfaceDeclaration(),
   interfaceFieldStatement(), interfaceMethodStatement(). *)
InterfaceDeclaration ::= 'interface' Identifier ( 'extends' QualifiedName )? EOS
                            InterfaceBody?
                         ( ( 'end' 'interface' ) | 'endinterface' )
InterfaceBody   ::= ( InterfaceMember EOS )* InterfaceMember?
InterfaceMember ::= AnnotatedInterfaceMember
                  | InterfaceField
                  | InterfaceMethod
                  | Comment
AnnotatedInterfaceMember ::= ( Annotation EOS )+ ( InterfaceField | InterfaceMethod )
InterfaceField  ::= 'optional'? Identifier 'as' Type
InterfaceMethod ::= 'optional'? ( 'function' | 'sub' )
                        Identifier LPAREN ParameterList? RPAREN ReturnType?

(*--- 2.4 Enum -------------------------------------------------------------*)

(* `enum Name ... end enum`. Members are `Name [= value]`; no backing-type
   clause in 0.72.2 (enumDeclaration does NOT parse `as Type`).
   BrighterScript-only. src/parser/Parser.ts: enumDeclaration(),
   enumMemberStatement(). *)
EnumDeclaration ::= 'enum' Identifier EOS
                        EnumBody?
                    ( ( 'end' 'enum' ) | 'endenum' )
EnumBody        ::= ( EnumMember EOS )* EnumMember?
EnumMember      ::= AnnotatedEnumMember | EnumMemberDecl | Comment
AnnotatedEnumMember ::= ( Annotation EOS )+ EnumMemberDecl
EnumMemberDecl  ::= Identifier ( ASSIGN Expression )?


(*===========================================================================*)
(*  PART 3 - OTHER BRIGHTERSCRIPT TOP-LEVEL / SCOPE STATEMENTS               *)
(*===========================================================================*)

(* `const NAME = expression` -- a compile-time constant (value is any
   expression). src/parser/Parser.ts: constDeclaration(). BrighterScript-only. *)
ConstStatement  ::= 'const' Identifier ASSIGN Expression

(* `import "pkg:/source/lib.bs"` -- pulls another file into scope.
   src/parser/Parser.ts: importStatement(). BrighterScript-only. *)
ImportStatement ::= 'import' StringLiteral

(* `typecast m as Type` -- scope-level assertion of the type of an identifier
   (typically `m`). The cast target is a single identifier, then `as Type`.
   src/parser/Parser.ts: typecastStatement(). BrighterScript-only. *)
TypecastStatement ::= 'typecast' Identifier 'as' Type

(* `alias NAME = VALUE`. NOTE: in 0.72.2 the value is a SINGLE identifier
   (aliasStatement consumes one identifier, not a dotted name) -- a known
   limitation of the early alias feature. src/parser/Parser.ts: aliasStatement().
   BrighterScript-only. *)
AliasStatement  ::= 'alias' Identifier ASSIGN Identifier

(* `type Name = TypeExpr` -- a type alias (e.g. `type Id = string or integer`).
   The value is a full BrighterScript type (Type, redefined below, includes
   unions). src/parser/Parser.ts: typeStatement(). BrighterScript-only. *)
TypeAliasStatement ::= 'type' Identifier ASSIGN Type


(*===========================================================================*)
(*  PART 4 - EXPRESSION EXTENSIONS (overrides woven into the cascade)         *)
(*===========================================================================*)

(* OVERRIDE of brightscript.ebnf Expression. The inherited cascade entry is
   OrExpr (and below). BrighterScript wraps it with, from outermost in:
     (1) type-cast `expr as Type` (chainable) -- applied last by the compiler;
     (2) ternary `cond ? a : b` and null-coalescing `a ?? b` (same level).
   Because this rule shadows the base `Expression`, every inherited position
   that referenced `Expression` (if/while/return/print/assignment RHS/args/...)
   now admits these forms automatically.
   src/parser/Parser.ts: expression() (wraps TypeCastExpression),
   anonymousFunction() (wraps Ternary/NullCoalescing), ternaryExpression(),
   nullCoalescingExpression(). All BrighterScript-only. *)
Expression      ::= ( TernaryExpr | NullCoalesceExpr ) ( 'as' Type )*  (* typecast outermost *)
TernaryExpr     ::= OrExpr ( QUESTION Expression COLON Expression )?   (* cond ? a : b; falls through to OrExpr *)
NullCoalesceExpr ::= OrExpr OP_NULLCOALESCE Expression                  (* a ?? b *)

(* OVERRIDE of brightscript.ebnf PostfixSuffix: adds the callfunc operator
   `@.method(args)` (transpiles to `.callFunc("method", args)`). The optional-
   chaining suffixes (?. ?@ ?[ ?( ) are already in the inherited OptChainSuffix
   (Roku OS 11+ runtime feature), so they are reused, not re-added.
   src/parser/Parser.ts: call() callfunc branch; Expression.ts:
   CallfuncExpression. CallfuncSuffix is BrighterScript-only. *)
PostfixSuffix   ::= CallSuffix
                  | IndexSuffix
                  | MemberSuffix
                  | AttributeSuffix
                  | OptChainSuffix
                  | CallfuncSuffix
CallfuncSuffix  ::= OP_CALLFUNC Identifier LPAREN ArgumentList? RPAREN

(* OVERRIDE of brightscript.ebnf Primary: adds the BrighterScript primary forms.
   The inherited alternatives are re-listed so this rule is complete.
   src/parser/Parser.ts: primary(). *)
Primary         ::= Literal
                  | Identifier
                  | 'm'
                  | ParenExpr
                  | ArrayLiteral
                  | AssocArrayLiteral
                  | AnonymousFunction
                  | CreateObjectCall
                  | BuiltinCall
                  (* --- BrighterScript-only primary forms --- *)
                  | NewExpression
                  | TemplateString
                  | TaggedTemplate
                  | RegexLiteral
                  | BsSourceLiteral

(* `new Qualified( args )` -- class instantiation. Parens are REQUIRED
   (newExpression consumes LeftParen or QuestionLeftParen). BrighterScript-only.
   src/parser/Parser.ts: newExpression(); Expression.ts: NewExpression. *)
NewExpression   ::= 'new' QualifiedName LPAREN ArgumentList? RPAREN

(* OVERRIDE of brightscript.ebnf AAEntry: adds COMPUTED keys `[ expr ]: value`
   alongside the inherited `key: value`. src/parser/Parser.ts: AA-literal branch
   of primary(); Expression.ts: AAIndexedMemberExpression. Computed-key form is
   BrighterScript-only. *)
AAEntry         ::= AAKey COLON Expression
                  | LBRACKET Expression RBRACKET COLON Expression

(*--- 4.1 Template strings (BrighterScript-only) ---------------------------*)

(* Backtick-delimited string with `${ expr }` interpolation and escape codes;
   transpiles to string concatenation / chr() calls. A TAGGED template is an
   identifier immediately (no space) followed by a template (a tag function).
   src/lexer/Lexer.ts: templateString(); src/parser/Parser.ts: templateString();
   Expression.ts: TemplateStringExpression / TaggedTemplateStringExpression. *)
TemplateString  ::= BACKTICK TemplateContent* BACKTICK
TemplateContent ::= TemplateChars | TemplateEscape | TemplateInterpolation
TemplateInterpolation ::= DOLLAR_LBRACE Expression RBRACE
TemplateChars   ::= ( Char - ( '`' | '\' | '$' ) )+
                    (* a bare '$' not followed by '{' is literal text -- a lexer
                       detail; see implementer note 4. *)
TemplateEscape  ::= '\' Char         (* \n \r \\ \" \cNNN (char code) etc. *)
TaggedTemplate  ::= Identifier TemplateString

(*--- 4.2 Regex literal (BrighterScript-only) ------------------------------*)

(* `/pattern/flags` -> CreateObject("roRegex", pattern, flags). Lexed only where
   a `/` cannot be division (start of expression / after an operator) -- a
   contextual lexer rule; see implementer note 5.
   src/lexer/Lexer.ts: regexLiteral(); Expression.ts: RegexLiteralExpression. *)
RegexLiteral    ::= '/' ( RegexChar | '\' Char )* '/' RegexFlags?
RegexChar       ::= Char - ( '/' | '\' | LINE_BREAK )
RegexFlags      ::= [a-zA-Z]+

(*--- 4.3 Source literals (BrighterScript-only) ----------------------------*)

(* Compiler-substituted source-position literals (BrighterScriptSourceLiterals,
   TokenKind.ts). `LINE_NUM` is NOT here -- it is available in plain BrightScript
   and lives in brightscript.ebnf's Literal. src/parser/Parser.ts: primary()
   source-literal branch; Expression.ts: SourceLiteralExpression. *)
BsSourceLiteral ::= 'source_file_path'
                  | 'source_line_num'
                  | 'function_name'
                  | 'source_function_name'
                  | 'source_namespace_name'
                  | 'source_namespace_root_name'
                  | 'source_location'
                  | 'pkg_path'
                  | 'pkg_location'


(*===========================================================================*)
(*  PART 5 - STATEMENT EXTENSIONS (typed forms, override seams)               *)
(*===========================================================================*)

(* OVERRIDE of brightscript.ebnf AssignmentStatement: adds the TYPED assignment
   `name as Type = value` (BrighterScript-only). The typed form applies to a
   bare identifier target (a semantic detail); AssignTarget is inherited.
   src/parser/Parser.ts: assignment(). *)
AssignmentStatement ::= AssignTarget ( 'as' Type )? ASSIGN Expression

(* OVERRIDE of brightscript.ebnf ForEachStatement: adds the TYPED loop item
   `for each x as Type in ...` (BrighterScript-only). Otherwise identical to the
   inherited rule. src/parser/Parser.ts: forEachStatement(). *)
ForEachStatement ::= 'for' 'each' Identifier ( 'as' Type )? 'in' Expression EOS
                        Block?
                     ( ( 'end' 'for' ) | 'endfor' )


(*===========================================================================*)
(*  PART 6 - TYPE GRAMMAR (override -- the BrighterScript `as` type language)  *)
(*===========================================================================*)

(* OVERRIDE of brightscript.ebnf Type. In plain `.brs` only the intrinsic type
   set is device-valid in an `as` clause (DEVICE_FACTS #6/#7); BrighterScript
   permits the full type language and lowers/erases it on transpile. Because
   this shadows the base `Type`, every inherited `as Type` position
   (params, return types, fields, typed assignment, typed for-each, casts)
   gains the BrighterScript type forms automatically.
   src/parser/Parser.ts: typeToken(); src/util.ts: tokenToBscType; src/types/*.

   Forms (lowest binding first):
     A or B / A and B      union/intersection types
     T[]                   typed array (repeatable: T[][])
     intrinsic | Custom | function(...)-type | { ... } | ( ... )   atoms        *)
Type            ::= BsTypeUnion
BsTypeUnion     ::= BsTypePostfix ( ( 'or' | 'and' ) BsTypePostfix )*
BsTypePostfix   ::= BsTypeAtom ( LBRACKET RBRACKET )*
BsTypeAtom      ::= IntrinsicType
                  | QualifiedName            (* custom / namespaced type name *)
                  | TypedFunctionType
                  | InlineInterfaceType
                  | GroupedType

(* The DeclarableTypes set (TokenKind.ts) -- intrinsic types nameable after `as`.
   These are also Identifiers, so QualifiedName would match them too; they are
   listed to document the intrinsic set (the compiler resolves the overlap). *)
IntrinsicType   ::= 'boolean' | 'integer' | 'longinteger' | 'float' | 'double'
                  | 'string' | 'object' | 'function' | 'dynamic' | 'void'
                  | 'invalid'

(* Callable type: `function(params) as Ret` / `sub(params) as Ret`.
   src/parser/Parser.ts: typedFunctionType(). *)
TypedFunctionType ::= ( 'function' | 'sub' ) LPAREN ParameterList? RPAREN ReturnType?

(* Anonymous (inline) interface type: `{ name as T, optional id as T }`.
   src/parser/Parser.ts: inlineInterface(). *)
InlineInterfaceType ::= LBRACE EOS?
                          ( InlineInterfaceField ( ElementSep InlineInterfaceField )* ElementSep? )?
                        EOS? RBRACE
InlineInterfaceField ::= 'optional'? Identifier 'as' Type

(* Parenthesized type: `( string or integer )`.
   src/parser/Parser.ts: groupedTypeExpression(). *)
GroupedType     ::= LPAREN Type RPAREN


(*===========================================================================*)
(*  PART 7 - LEXICAL TOKENS ADDED BY BRIGHTERSCRIPT                           *)
(*===========================================================================*)

(* Operators / punctuation not present in brightscript.ebnf. CASE-INSENSITIVE
   like all BrightScript tokens. Longest-match ordering vs the inherited tokens
   is in implementer note 2. src/lexer/TokenKind.ts. *)
OP_NULLCOALESCE ::= '??'              (* QuestionQuestion *)
OP_CALLFUNC     ::= '@.'             (* Callfunc -- node@.method(...) *)
BACKTICK        ::= '`'              (* template-string delimiter *)
DOLLAR_LBRACE   ::= '${'            (* template interpolation opener *)


(*===========================================================================*)
(*  PART 8 - NOTES FOR THE TREE-SITTER IMPLEMENTER                            *)
(*===========================================================================*)
(*
  These extend brightscript.ebnf's implementer notes; everything there (case-
  insensitivity, significant newlines / bracket-depth scanner, maximal-munch
  ordering, the type-suffix lexing) still applies. BrighterScript adds:

  1. SUPERSET / INJECTION SCOPE.
     A `.bs` file is parsed with the BrighterScript grammar; a `.brs` file with
     the BrightScript grammar. In SceneGraph, inject the BrighterScript grammar
     (not just BrightScript) into a <script> whose type is brighterscript / whose
     `uri` ends in `.bs` (scenegraph.ebnf marks the embedding point; the chosen
     injected grammar depends on the script's language).

  2. THE `@` TOKEN IS OVERLOADED -- disambiguate by context:
       - `@.`  callfunc operator   (OP_CALLFUNC), only mid-expression after a
               value:  node@.doIt(1).
       - `@Name` annotation        (AT + identifier) at the START of a
               declaration / statement position.
       - `@attr` XML-attribute get (inherited AttributeSuffix) mid-expression.
       - `?@`  optional XML-attribute get (inherited OptChainSuffix).
     The lexer emits `@.` (callfunc) maximally; a bare `@` is annotation or
     attribute-get per position. Longest-match: `@.` before `@`.

  3. `as <CustomType>` IS VALID IN `.bs` (unlike `.brs`).
     brightscript.ebnf restricts the device-valid `as` set to intrinsics
     (DEVICE_FACTS #6/#7); here Type is overridden to admit custom/namespaced
     names, `T[]`, unions, function- and inline-interface types. On transpile
     these are erased/lowered, so the emitted `.brs` only ever carries intrinsic
     (or no) `as` annotations -- which is what the DEVICE then validates.

  4. TEMPLATE STRINGS need a dedicated lexer mode entered on BACKTICK:
       - literal runs -> TemplateChars; `${` opens an interpolation that lexes a
         full nested expression until the matching `}`; backtick closes.
       - escapes inside: \n \r \\ \" and \cNNN (unicode char code); a physical
         newline is allowed and becomes a char-code literal.
       - a `$` not followed by `{` is literal text.
       - TAGGED template = Identifier immediately (no whitespace) before the
         opening backtick.

  5. REGEX LITERAL `/.../flags` is CONTEXTUAL: lex a regex (not division) only
     when the preceding significant token cannot end an expression (start of
     statement/expression, or right after an operator/`(`/`,`/`return`/etc.).
     Inside, `\` escapes the next char; the closing `/` ends the body; a
     trailing run of letters is the flags. (Mirrors src/lexer/Lexer.ts
     PreceedingRegexTypes.)

  6. CONTEXTUAL KEYWORDS. Most BrighterScript keywords (class, namespace,
     interface, enum, const, import, typecast, alias, type, new, public,
     protected, private, optional, override, as) are CONTEXTUAL: they are also
     valid identifiers / member names / AA keys in other positions
     (AllowedLocalIdentifiers / AllowedProperties in TokenKind.ts). The grammar
     treats them as keywords in declaration position and as Identifier elsewhere;
     a scanner-gated approach (as used for BrightScript keyword disambiguation)
     is required. In particular `optional` and `override` can themselves be field
     / member names (the parser uses look-ahead/rewind).

  7. `extends` / `in` / `each` / `override` are matched by literal text in the
     parser (not all are distinct TokenKinds) -- keep them case-insensitive.

  8. DEVICE VALIDATION IS VIA TRANSPILE. BrighterScript constructs are confirmed
     on hardware by transpiling `.bs` -> `.brs`, sideloading, and reading
     `##SPEC##` (see roadmap/05 Phase 4). The grammar models source `.bs`; the
     thing that RUNS on the Roku is the lowered `.brs` already covered by
     brightscript.ebnf. Record device-confirmed lowering facts in DEVICE_FACTS.md.
*)
